                            jcr:mixinTypes="[cq:LiveRelationship]"
                            jcr:primaryType="nt:unstructured"
                            sling:resourceType="weekender/components/contentfragment"
                            displayMode="singleText"
                            elementNames="itinerary"
                            fragmentPath="/content/dam/weekender-shared/en/adventures/west-coast-cycling/west-coast-cycling"
                            paragraphScope="all"
                            text="West Coast Cycling Days 1 and 2: Bridge, cliffs and redwoods We roll out over the Golden Gate Bridge and follow the coast road north, high above the sea. On the second day the route turns inland through a forest of redwoods, on a quiet road where the trees stand close enough to touch. Days 3 and 4: The Oregon coast Across the state line the shore becomes a string of headlands, sea stacks and long empty beaches, with a lighthouse every few hours. We sleep in small harbour towns and eat what the boats bring in. Day 5: Inland to Portland The last stage leaves the sea and crosses the coastal hills through farmland and vineyards to Portland, where the trip ends with dinner in the city."
                            variationName="master">
                            <par6
